# Smart Mechatronic Asset Monitoring & Edge Data Platform

## 1. Project Overview

This project is an IoT, Mechatronics, Data Engineering, Backend, and Frontend platform built around the hardware already available:

- Raspberry Pi 4
- Arduino Uno-compatible board
- DC geared motor
- L298N motor driver
- DHT11
- DHT22
- HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor
- PIR motion sensor
- MQ-series gas sensor
- Buzzer
- LEDs
- IR receiver
- IR remote control
- Bluetooth module
- Breadboard
- Jumper wires
- Resistors
- Battery / power supply

The goal is to build a small connected mechatronic machine capable of:

- controlling a motor;
- monitoring its operating environment;
- detecting obstacles and human presence;
- generating real-time telemetry;
- producing safety events and alerts;
- storing historical data;
- exposing data through a backend API;
- displaying system status in a frontend dashboard;
- creating analytics and anomaly detection workflows.

The project is designed so that a future version can evolve naturally into a full **Industrial Predictive Maintenance Platform**.

---

# 2. Main Objective

The goal is to build an end-to-end platform following this architecture:

```text
Physical Machine
      ↓
Sensors + Arduino
      ↓
Raspberry Pi 4
      ↓
    MQTT
      ↓
Data Ingestion
      ↓
Real-Time Storage
      ↓
Historical Data Lake
      ↓
Transformation / Analytics
      ↓
Backend API
      ↓
Frontend Dashboard
      ↓
Alerts / Anomaly Detection
```

The platform will allow us to:

- start and stop the motor;
- change motor direction;
- control motor speed;
- monitor temperature and humidity;
- detect obstacles;
- detect human presence;
- monitor a gas/environment value;
- activate visual and audible alarms;
- generate machine events;
- persist all telemetry;
- analyze the machine's history;
- build operational KPIs;
- detect unusual behavior.

