# 5. Motor Control

The Arduino controls the DC motor through the L298N.

```text
Arduino
   │
   ├── PWM
   ├── Direction A
   └── Direction B
          ↓
        L298N
          ↓
      DC Motor
```

The system should support:

```text
STOP
FORWARD
REVERSE

25%
50%
75%
100%
```

or equivalent PWM-based speed levels.

> Important: the motor voltage must be verified before connecting the 12 V battery. Many TT geared motors are designed for lower voltages such as 3–6 V.

The Raspberry Pi should also use an appropriate independent power supply.

