# 7. HC-SR04 — Obstacle Detection

The HC-SR04 measures distance.

Example:

```text
Distance = 92 cm
Distance = 71 cm
Distance = 43 cm
Distance = 14 cm
```

A safety rule can be created:

```text
distance < 20 cm
        ↓
Obstacle detected
        ↓
Stop motor
        ↓
Create event
        ↓
Send MQTT alert
```

This introduces automated safety logic and event-driven behavior.

---

# 8. PIR — Presence Detection

The PIR sensor detects human motion or presence.

Example:

```text
presence = TRUE
```

Possible industrial safety logic:

```text
Person detected
      ↓
Safety event
      ↓
Stop motor
      ↓
Buzzer
      ↓
Alert
      ↓
Event stored
```

---

# 9. MQ-Series Sensor — Environmental Monitoring

The MQ-series module can initially provide a raw gas/environment measurement.

Example:

```text
gas_raw = 284
```

Later, thresholds can classify the state:

```text
NORMAL
WARNING
CRITICAL
```

The exact MQ model should be identified before interpreting the value as a specific gas concentration.

---

# 10. DHT22 and DHT11

The DHT22 will be the main environmental sensor.

It provides:

```text
temperature
humidity
```

Example:

```text
temperature = 25.7 °C
humidity = 51 %
```

The DHT11 can be used as:

- a secondary measurement point;
- a comparison sensor;
- an environmental redundancy experiment.

---

# 11. LEDs and Buzzer

The LEDs and buzzer represent machine status locally.

Example:

```text
GREEN LED
↓
NORMAL

YELLOW LED
↓
WARNING

RED LED
+
BUZZER
↓
CRITICAL
```

The same status will also be sent to the data platform.

---

# 12. IR Remote Control

The IR remote and receiver can provide local machine commands.

Example mapping:

```text
1 → Start
2 → Stop
3 → Forward
4 → Reverse

▲ → Increase speed
▼ → Reduce speed
```

Commands should also generate events:

```text
14:30:04 USER_COMMAND START
14:30:07 MOTOR_STARTED
14:32:11 OBSTACLE_DETECTED
14:32:11 EMERGENCY_STOP
```

This creates useful event logs for analytics.

---

# 13. Raspberry Pi 4 — Edge Gateway

The Raspberry Pi acts as the Edge Gateway.

Responsibilities:

```text
Arduino Serial Reader
        ↓
Validation
        ↓
MQTT Publisher
        ↓
Local Buffering
        ↓
Edge Processing
```

It may host:

- Mosquitto;
- Python collector;
- InfluxDB;
- Grafana;
- Docker services;
- local logs and buffering.

