# 15. Data Architecture

The platform will use:

```text
RAW
 ↓
SILVER
 ↓
GOLD
```

## RAW

Raw telemetry exactly as received from the Raspberry Pi.

Possible fields:

```text
timestamp
device_id
temperature
humidity
distance
presence
gas_raw
motor_state
motor_command
```

Minimal transformation should occur here.

## SILVER

The data becomes:

- correctly typed;
- cleaned;
- deduplicated;
- validated;
- timestamp-normalized;
- checked for impossible values.

## GOLD

Business- and analytics-ready datasets.

Possible fields:

```text
machine_hourly_metrics

avg_temperature
max_temperature
avg_humidity
obstacle_count
presence_count
motor_runtime
stop_count
alarm_count
gas_avg
gas_max
```

---

# 16. Data Quality

Data quality rules will detect invalid or suspicious values.

Examples:

```text
temperature = 250 °C
→ INVALID

humidity = -15 %
→ INVALID

distance = -1 cm
→ SENSOR ERROR

same event duplicated
→ DUPLICATE

timestamp missing
→ INVALID

sensor did not send data for 30 seconds
→ SENSOR OFFLINE
```

Invalid data may be routed to:

```text
data/quarantine/
```

